WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical narration text; deterministic paragraph-window timing.
Text and terminology reviewed against the chapter packet on 2026-07-29.
Publication still requires final listening review against the authorized narration master.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.803
A capable component is not a light bulb that can be

2
00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:08.151
unscrewed and replaced. It may carry model weights,

3
00:00:08.151 --> 00:00:12.754
optimizer and scheduler state, random-number state, caches, credentials, policies, routes, backups,

4
00:00:12.754 --> 00:00:16.102
descendants, and commitments already made outside the machine.

5
00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:20.705
A replacement can look successful while half of that world still

6
00:00:20.705 --> 00:00:25.309
belongs to the old version. This chapter therefore treats replacement as

7
00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:29.075
a governed transaction over one declared Stable Capability Field.

8
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:33.260
The transaction names the prior implementation, candidate, consumers, authority, evidence,

9
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.863
recovery objective, and every state or effect surface before the result

10
00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:38.700
is known.

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.002
The first discipline is prospective identity. Before evaluation,

12
00:00:43.002 --> 00:00:47.756
freeze the field version, prior and candidate digests, dependency graph,

13
00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:52.509
change class, checkpoint authority, evaluator, monitor, canary scope, thresholds, owners,

14
00:00:52.509 --> 00:00:57.737
and expiry. Then inventory state and effects. Model parameters are only

15
00:00:57.737 --> 00:01:02.965
one row. Optimizer, scheduler, random-number generator, cache, backup, credential, policy, receipt,

16
00:01:02.965 --> 00:01:08.194
data, route, monitor, descendant, and external commitment need explicit rows too.

17
00:01:08.194 --> 00:01:13.422
Effects are classified as reversible, replayable, compensatable, forked, disclosure-like, externally owned,

18
00:01:13.422 --> 00:01:17.700
or irreversible. Anything omitted cannot later be called recovered.

19
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.194
The candidate then moves through explicit states: proposed, precheck, isolated shadow,

20
00:01:23.194 --> 00:01:27.734
bounded canary, default candidate, committed, monitored, rolled back, compensated, quarantined,

21
00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:32.729
or retired. Shadow and canary routes have bounded data, tools, writes,

22
00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:37.723
network access, learning, and external effects. Qualification includes usefulness, historical regressions,

23
00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:42.263
critical-failure vetoes, adversarial cases, authority and rights preservation, state compatibility,

24
00:01:42.263 --> 00:01:47.257
complete cost, and transfer. The candidate cannot be its own sole

25
00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:51.344
proposer, evaluator, promoter, monitor, incident judge, and rollback authority.

26
00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:56.338
Shared dependencies are recorded because independence is a property to measure,

27
00:01:56.338 --> 00:01:57.700
not a label.

28
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.985
Imagine replacing a planning kernel. The current route is version A.

29
00:02:02.985 --> 00:02:07.770
Version B passes prechecks and enters a five-percent canary without permission

30
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:11.250
to train descendants or mutate the default cache.

31
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:16.035
A delayed monitor detects a critical regression. The stop condition prevents

32
00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:20.820
default promotion. Recovery restores the prospectively chosen checkpoint and route A,

33
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.170
then compares every declared state surface with its recovery objective.

34
00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.650
A changed remote copy cannot be reversed locally,

35
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:33.435
so the transaction assigns compensation and an owner instead of announcing

36
00:02:33.435 --> 00:02:37.785
success. The terminal receipt records the failed candidate, the rollback,

37
00:02:37.785 --> 00:02:41.700
the unresolved external effect, cost, and every affected descendant.

38
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.835
This example separates six commonly collapsed outcomes. Restoring artifact bytes is

39
00:02:46.835 --> 00:02:51.470
not restoring all state. Restarting a service is not recovering behavior.

40
00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.683
Digest equality is not privacy repair. Compensation is not reversal.

41
00:02:55.683 --> 00:03:00.318
A receipt is not independent observation. And one exact local inventory

42
00:03:00.318 --> 00:03:03.689
is not proof that the inventory was complete.

43
00:03:03.689 --> 00:03:07.902
The strongest failure modes follow directly: checkpoint hindsight, regression deletion,

44
00:03:07.902 --> 00:03:12.116
evaluator capture, canary contamination, monitor blindness, partial commit, forward-only migration,

45
00:03:12.116 --> 00:03:15.487
authority smuggling, rollback theater, irreversibility laundering, rollback cascades,

46
00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:19.700
and repeated promote-rollback trials that hide accumulated cost and residuals.

47
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.938
The chapter has real but narrow evidence. One prospective local campaign

48
00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:28.383
restored fifteen of fifteen declared transaction trees exactly,

49
00:03:28.383 --> 00:03:33.121
while six best-versus-final checkpoint disagreements showed why checkpoint authority must be

50
00:03:33.121 --> 00:03:37.858
fixed in advance. Another attack-control campaign achieved exact rollback in thirty-two

51
00:03:37.858 --> 00:03:42.596
of thirty-six cases but admitted useful release in only two of

52
00:03:42.596 --> 00:03:47.334
thirty-six, below both release gates. A larger bounded inventory exercise restored

53
00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:52.071
thirty-five of thirty-five named local surfaces, while immutable corpus, feature, checkpoint,

54
00:03:52.071 --> 00:03:56.378
raw-evidence, simulated remote, and external-descendant surfaces remained unresolved by design.

55
00:03:56.378 --> 00:04:00.254
These are useful tests of record and recovery discipline,

56
00:04:00.254 --> 00:04:03.700
not proof of production usefulness or effect-complete rollback.

57
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.700
The core claim therefore remains Design rationale at argument support.

58
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.650
The maximum justified inference is bounded local non-core governance effect only.

59
00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:18.150
This visual does not establish a useful replacement, production transfer,

60
00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:22.200
semantic recovery, privacy erasure, independent evaluator quality, safe self-improvement,

61
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.800
or chapter-core promotion. The practical rule is simple:

62
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.750
no replacement is complete until identity, evidence, state, effects, authority, recovery,

63
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.700
residuals, descendants, and terminal disposition are all explicit. The next chapter,

64
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.650
Security Kernel and Digital SCIFs, asks how privileged execution can remain

65
00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.700
isolated while those replacement and recovery obligations are enforced.
